#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""tier-pick-audit — M-588 B4: read-only audit of the tier-pick inputs.

The M-423 resolver picks a tier by `important_level` + `complexity` (issue
custom properties) and a role quality floor. M-424 supplies the model quality
ranking. Both are inert if the values are missing. This tool measures how much
is missing and reports what it can and cannot resolve through the same read
path the M-577 scorecard uses: the `multica` CLI, nothing else.

Read-only contract:
  * every number comes from `multica issue list`, `multica property list` or
    `multica agent list` (or a pre-captured fixture);
  * no DB/curl, no writes to the board, no comments, no status changes;
  * a metric with no CLI read path is listed in `unavailable[]` with the
    missing field — never estimated, never invented;
  * no LLM is called anywhere in this path.

Sources (also in README.md):
  issues + difficulty  `multica issue list --resolve-properties --output json`
                       (paged at 100; `properties[]` carries name + value)
  property ids/usage   `multica property list --output json`
  agent role mapping   `multica agent list --output json` (`tier_role`)
  tier quality / cost / role links / manual_only / online runtime /
  model_tier_role      NO CLI READ PATH — see `unavailable[]`

Usage:
  tier-pick-audit [--date YYYY-MM-DD] [--out-dir DIR] [--stdout]
                  [--fixture captured.json] [--cli /path/to/multica]
                  [--dry-run]

Exit codes: 0 report written, 2 bad usage / unreadable input.
"""

